# Brick Breaker v2

25 levels, star-gated tiers, coin shop, procedural backgrounds.

## Build an APK to share

**Windows:** double-click `build-release.bat`
**macOS / Linux:** `./build-release.sh`

Result: `BrickBreaker-v2.0.apk` in this folder. Send it to anyone.

### You need first

- **JDK 17** — not 21. The Gradle 8.2.1 wrapper here supports Java 8–20;
  JDK 21 fails with *Unsupported class file major version 65*.
  Get it from https://adoptium.net
- **Android Studio** — for the SDK. Install it, open the `android` folder
  once, then close it.
- **Node.js** — https://nodejs.org

First build downloads ~1 GB and takes 10–20 minutes. After that, seconds.

### The keystore

`build-release.bat` creates `android/brickbreaker.jks` on first run and asks
you for a password.

**Back that file up somewhere safe.** Android identifies an app by its
signing key. Lose the keystore and you cannot ship an update — every phone
and the Play Store will treat a re-signed build as a different app, and the
only way forward is a new listing under a new package name.

It is gitignored, along with the password file, so neither ends up in
version control.

## Other builds

| Command | Output | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `build-release.bat` | signed APK | sharing directly |
| `build-apk.bat` | debug APK | quick testing, no keystore |
| `cd android && gradlew bundleRelease` | `.aab` | Play Store upload |

## Files

| | |
|---|---|
| `www/index.html` | the whole game, self-contained |
| `android/` | Capacitor wrapper |
| `BUILD_APK.md` | detailed build and signing notes |
| `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` | what's fixed, what isn't |

## Before submitting to Play

1. Add back-button handling — see `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`. Right now the back
   button exits the app mid-game.
2. Check the current target API requirement. `targetSdkVersion` is 34 and
   Google raises the floor annually; a stale target is a hard rejection.
3. Bump `versionCode` in `android/app/build.gradle` on every upload.
